# Force LF for tracked Python source - Windows checkouts must not silently gain CRLF (git's
# own core.autocrlf conversion) on files migration writers/tests compare byte-for-byte, and
# generated migrations under */migrations/ are always written with explicit LF (see
# hare/migrations/writer.py's MigrationWriter.write()) regardless of the platform that ran
# makemigrations.
*.py text eol=lf

# Shell scripts run inside Linux containers (tests/docker) - a CRLF line ending breaks their shebang.
*.sh text eol=lf
